I won!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! My first victory. After some 6 month of
playing nethack, my first victory. 

Now that the spell is broken I can go back to my thesis. But first
some spoilers for those still trying to win their first game.



I usually play barbarian. It seems to be the most appropriate character
for  my style of playing, which is just muscle and no brains. 
The advantage of the barbarian is that it starts with poison resistance,
so you can eat any corpse you find around. There is little chance of
dying of starvation, and because you eat every corpse
you will soon get fire and cold resistance.

At experience 7, the barbarian gets speed which is really important at
lower levels. With that speed I find myself a non-aligned unicorn and kill it.
It takes some time and patience but it can be done. Once with the unicorn
horn I quaff all the potions I have collected so far.

I hang around altars until I get the stormbringer from the gods. It seems that
you will not receive any more powerful weapon from the gods. 
Talking about weapons, I cannot praise enough a heavy ball as a weapon:
with luck you get it soon, it is rust proof, and it is a VERY good weapon. 
I used as my sole weapon trough out this game I won.

As for armor, I won this game with a AC -8, nothing fancy. The only
creatures that you have to look for are the minotaur and them ochre/spotted
jellies, and I am not sure if a better AC will even help with the jellies.
(I hate ochre jellies !). I also tend to prefer rust proof
armor. Thus although a hard hat is better then a leather hat I will keep
the latter, so that I dont have to worry with rust traps and rust monsters.
As for shields I think the blue and green elf shield is rust proof.
I used one of my wishes to get a reflection shield. It is handy when
fighting dragons. To go to the labyrinth some magic protection is a must:
it will protect you from polymorph traps and it will give some protection 
against liches (L). (BTY, liches are a very good choice for a blessed
genocide scroll).

As for intrinsics and other abilities, I find extremely useful
to have  teleport and teleport control abilities. I will look for a
teleport control ring and even use a wish to get one. Then I will eat 
something that makes you feel jumpy. This will allow you to teletransport
out of danger. But dont wait too much until your hit points are too low
because then you  wont have enough strength to teletransport. It also allow
you to appear next to a monster, hit it, and get out. That is what I did 
with the minotaur, which seems to be the only creature that can kill
you before you kill it (at least with and AC -8).

Levitation is a GREAT ability: either a ring of levitation or a non-cursed
levitation boot. It is great to just fly over moats and the such. 
But the great thing about levitation (here comes a BIG SPOILER) is

to engrave Elbereth and levitate over it. The monsters can only hit you with
projectiles and boulders, but you can hit them as you wish. This makes the
game really easy. Also levitation takes all the worry from the drawbridge.
You just *hit* the drawbridge and levitate over the moat.


To get to the labyrinth levels, let me remind you that there seems  always
 to be a level teletransport trap at or above the medusa level.

Finally some fortunes that summarize some of my recent experiences:

   Never fight a lich with your blindfold on.

   Never carry important potions or scrolls in levels where the creatures
   can spit fire at you.

   Always remove and drop all rings and wands before opening a chest or
   box.

   Always try any kind of key at the doors. 


That is it. Now that the spell is broken I'll rm -r my nethack directory
and go on with my thesis.

All the luck to you all nethacker

